+# 229 — F2 hardening after M3 re-review
 
-Date: 2026-11-09
+Date: 2026-11-09, corrected 2026-11-10
 
 The initial basename denylist was bypassable. Replaced with key-file identity
 checks:
 
 ```text
 is_secret_file(path):
+  literal protected names (assistant.key/.env/session.token) and aliases
   resolve equality
   os.path.samefile (hardlinks/case aliases)
   normalized basename (Windows trailing dot/space/default stream spelling)
@@ -17,8 +18,19 @@ Applied to:
 ```text
 app/services/attempt_writer.py
 tools/routea_bundle_to_attempt.py (single and multi-evidence zip)
-tools/route_bundle_ingest.py
+tools/route_bundle_ingest.py — guard added; this module has no active product
+                              call path (do not claim runtime coverage)
 ```
 
-Custom `BINARYREPAIR_ASSISTANT_KEY_FILE` paths and hardlinks are covered.
-Tests: full suite pass.
+## N-10 (accepted limitation)
+
+A custom `BINARYREPAIR_ASSISTANT_KEY_FILE` is protected only when the adapter
+process sees the same env. The default filename `assistant.key` is always
+rejected regardless of env. Multi-process custom-env deployments must set the
+same env or use the default path.
+
+## N-11 correction
+
+No claim that `route_bundle_ingest` is exercised by the product. Full-suite
+numbers are platform-scoped: 741/739/2 on this macOS run; Windows M3 used
+66/740 with e2e environment skips.
